#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""aimail — unified maintenance CLI for the aimail agent-integration stack.

Subcommands (grouped by scenario, see --help):
  setup      init / install / uninstall / reset
  operate    stats / renew / version
  diagnose   check / repair / ping / welcome / persona
  resources  domain / address / bridge

Platform fact inference (no --agent-type, per 2026-08-16 ruling):
  1. --home given → directory traits (hermes-agent|profiles=hermes,
     openclaw.json=openclaw, .dsh+profiles/storages=dsh, .pi+agent=pi,
     backend/app/gateway=deerflow)
  2. --system-id → config system_home reverse lookup → directory traits
     (legacy: pointer ownership fallback)
  3. neither → auto-probe first platform with a .agentmail pointer

Semantics:
  system_home = platform root (hermes=~/.hermes, openclaw=~/.openclaw, ...)
  agent_home  = concrete agent home (adapter-internal, never a subcommand arg)
  Endpoint/config contracts (inbound path /aimail/inbound, agentmail.json
  9 fields, aimail_gateway.json) have their single source of truth in the
  TS SDK (tssdk/) — python code references it, never redefines.
"""
